<div class="guide-styles" data-ay-injected="true" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for Feral Druid Tank in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Icecrown Citadel on 25-man Heroic difficulty, with listed alternatives from the 10-man and Normal difficulty versions of the raid as well. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Feral Druid Tank Phase 4</h2>Phase 4 marks the first time in WotLK that gearing priorities for Feral tanks will deviate from simply maximizing Item Level and Stamina in every single gear slot, even though these two attributes remain the most impactful characteristics for overall tanking value in any single item slot. The main source of deviation comes from the fact that the 4-piece <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-845/lasherweave-battlegear">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Lasherweave Battlegear</span></a> set bonus is so overpowered for survivability on <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> raid encounters that completing the set takes priority over any other gearing considerations. In fact, simulation comparisons conclusively show that even the base version of the Tier 10 set, which is only 251 Item Level and where every piece individually is worse than even <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/tank-bis-gear-pve-phase-3">Phase 3 BiS gear</a>, is worth using over the best 277 Item Level off-piece options from 25-man Heroic ICC, simply due to the power of the bonus. The reason for such high importance given to the 4pT10 bonus comes from the damage profiles of the hardest ICC bosses, which center around timed "tank buster" abilities like <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36853/sindragosa">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa</span></a>'s <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69649/frost-breath">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostnova.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Breath</span></a> and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36597/the-lich-king">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Lich King</span></a>'s <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69409/soul-reaper">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_shadowdance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Reaper</span></a>, which are <i>designed</i> to not be consistently survivable even in endgame BiS gear without having one or more defensive cooldowns active when the ability goes off. As a result, unlocking the ability to utilize <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=5229/enrage">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_enrage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enrage</span></a> as another 1-minute defensive cooldown in your arsenal is insanely valuable for comfortably surviving these encounters. Bears are especially reliant on the set bonus compared to other tanks because they possess fewer total cooldown options in their base toolkit, and specifically lack any 2-minute cooldowns like <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48792/icebound-fortitude">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_iceboundfortitude.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Icebound Fortitude</span></a> and <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45747/glyph-of-salvation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glyph_majorpaladin.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Salvation</span></a> that can fill in missing gaps in their CD rotation.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="general-survival">General Survival Set</h3>The first gear set shown just below is a generic maximum survival configuration that is appropriate for tanking the large majority of bosses in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>, including <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36597/the-lich-king">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Lich King</span></a> himself:<br/>
