<div class="slider-labels">
<span class="slider-labels-title">Level</span>
<span class="slider-labels-values">
<span class="slider-labels-values-sizer">80</span>
<input class="slider-labels-values-input" data-field-filled="true" disabled="" style="width: 20px;" type="text"/>
<span class="slider-labels-values-max">80</span></span></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<br/>When fully raid buffed with consumables, a bear wearing the above set will achieve the following tank metrics:<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">71,781 HP (<i>far</i> more than any other tank spec)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">45,060 armor</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">43.3% avoidance (with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69127/chill-of-the-throne">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_zone_icecrown_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chill of the Throne</span></a>)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">12,171 TPS</div></li></ul>The ability to access such a sky-high effective health pool (EHP) makes Feral Druids a phenomenal tank choice for the hardest hitting bosses in ICC, including <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=37813/deathbringer-saurfang">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer Saurfang</span></a>, <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36626/festergut">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Festergut</span></a>, and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36597/the-lich-king">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Lich King</span></a>, especially because the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69127/chill-of-the-throne">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_zone_icecrown_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chill of the Throne</span></a> debuff in ICC combined with the consistently slow boss swing timers across the instance favors EHP-based tanks over avoidance and Block-based tanks. Furthermore, all of these encounters feature taunt swap mechanics where two tanks will alternate between actively tanking the boss and DPSing, so the fact that the <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-253/sanctified-lasherweave-battlegear">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sanctified Lasherweave Battlegear</span></a> set bonuses provide immense DPS boosts while in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=768/cat-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a>, in addition to their Threat and survivability benefits in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=9634/dire-bear-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_bearform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dire Bear Form</span></a>, synergizes incredibly well with ICC encounters.<br/>
<br/>Note that the BiS setup includes the Engineering-exclusive enchants <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=63770/reticulated-armor-webbing">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reticulated Armor Webbing</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67839/mind-amplification-dish">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mind Amplification Dish</span></a>. As mentioned in our <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/tank-overview-pve#best-professions">class overview guide</a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=202/engineering">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> is such an insanely overpowered profession for PvE that it is assumed that any competitive Feral tank player will have it. In contrast, your second profession choice has hardly any impact in WotLK since all crafting professions provide very comparable PvE benefits, so no other profession-exclusive gear augmentations are assumed.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="sindragosa">Sindragosa Frost Resistance Set</h3>While the above gear set will be optimal for tanking almost all of ICC, this guide also includes a second specialized gear set optimized for tanking the <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36853/sindragosa">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa</span></a> encounter, which has some unique gearing considerations relative to the rest of the instance. Firstly, unlike most WotLK raid bosses, Sindragosa exhibits the "Parry Haste" property, which means that her (normally slow) swing timer gets sped up whenever she parries an incoming melee attack. While bears are naturally better equipped to deal with this mechanic than other tanks, since they are the only tank spec that is guaranteed to passively live two sequential melee swings from the boss without a heal in Phase 3 gear, Parry Haste still elevates the value of Expertise for bears on Sindragosa relative to other encounters. In particular, using <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50678/seal-of-many-mouths">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_icecrownringc.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Seal of Many Mouths</span></a> in place of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50404/ashen-band-of-endless-courage">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_84.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ashen Band of Endless Courage</span></a>, <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42994/rhinolicious-wormsteak">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_food_47.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rhinolicious Wormsteak</span></a> in place of <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42999/blackened-dragonfin">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_food_142_fish.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blackened Dragonfin</span></a>, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40141/guardians-dreadstone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_40.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Guardian's Dreadstone</span></a> in place of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40130/shifting-dreadstone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_40.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shifting Dreadstone</span></a> are efficient Expertise swaps relative to the general BiS setup that will reduce the frequency of Parry Haste sequences without compromising overall survivability. For early progression kills, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47063/pride-of-the-eredar">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pride of the Eredar</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47436/pride-of-the-demon-lord">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_18.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pride of the Demon Lord</span></a> can be used in lieu of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47549/magnis-resolution">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Magni's Resolution</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47550/cairnes-endurance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_18.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cairne's Endurance</span></a> for the same purpose.<br/>
<br/>Secondly, while <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36853/sindragosa">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa</span></a> does hit extremely hard like other ICC bosses, the most likely cause of deaths on this encounter for Feral tanks in particular will be her signature tank buster <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69649/frost-breath">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostnova.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Breath</span></a>, which deals exclusively Frost damage that cannot be mitigated by Armor but <i>can</i> be partially resisted. Since <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69649/frost-breath">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostnova.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Breath</span></a> is cast around every 22 seconds, the strongest bear cooldowns for it like <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=22812/barkskin">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_stoneclawtotem.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Barkskin</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=61336/survival-instincts">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_tigersroar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Survival Instincts</span></a> will not always be available to either mitigate the damage or guarantee survival on an unmitigated hit. As a result, wearing a hefty amount of Frost Resistance gear is highly recommended for Feral tanks on this fight in order to provide passive damage mitigation against the breath and guarantee survival against a breath + melee damage sequence even without a personal or external cooldown available. A side benefit of stacking Frost Resistance as a tank is that it will also mitigate the smaller sources of continuous Frost damage taken throughout the fight from the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70084/frost-aura">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostshock.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Aura</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70107/permeating-chill">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_coldhearted.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Permeating Chill</span></a> mechanics.<br/>
<br/>The gear set shown below incorporates both of these gearing considerations self-consistently, and was optimized using simulations to provide the lowest attainable chance of death on Sindragosa:<br/>
