<div id="guide-body-article-au__ayManagerEnv__1"></div></div>
<br/>When combined with a Frost Resistance raid buff (either <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48945/frost-resistance-aura">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_wizardmark.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Resistance Aura</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=58745/frost-resistance-totem">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frostresistancetotem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Resistance Totem</span></a>), this setup achieves 462 FrR, which corresponds to 47.5% average mitigation of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69649/frost-breath">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostnova.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Breath</span></a> damage. While even higher FrR values are technically achievable, the swaps required for this are net survivability losses for the encounter as a whole, since they give up too much physical EHP (which is still very important given how hard the boss hits with melee attacks). In particular, it is sometimes recommended for players to use <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44939/lesser-flask-of-resistance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_potion_118.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lesser Flask of Resistance</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=57694/fur-lining-frost-resist">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fur Lining - Frost Resist</span></a> when tanking Sindragosa, but simulation comparisons have demonstrated that both of these swaps are suboptimal: the combination of <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40076/gurus-elixir">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_potion_112.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Guru's Elixir</span></a> + <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40097/elixir-of-protection">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_alchemy_potion_empty.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elixir of Protection</span></a> provides more overall survivability than <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44939/lesser-flask-of-resistance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_potion_118.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lesser Flask of Resistance</span></a> does, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=57690/fur-lining-stamina">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fur Lining - Stamina</span></a> is in fact the preferred bracer enchant for Leatherworkers. In contrast, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=41377/effulgent-skyflare-diamond">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_icediamond_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Effulgent Skyflare Diamond</span></a>, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44137/arcanum-of-the-frosty-soul">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frozencore.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of the Frosty Soul</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44483/enchant-cloak-superior-frost-resistance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulagood_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Cloak - Superior Frost Resistance</span></a>, and all three pieces of the leather crafted Frost Resistance set are worth swapping in as net survivability gains for this encounter, even when you are fully decked out in ICC BiS gear.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="farm-content">Balanced Set for Farm Content</h3>Finally, as part of our content updates for the upcoming release of <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4987/the-ruby-sanctum">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Ruby Sanctum</span></a>, a third "balanced" setup has been added below as an example for readers who are already farming ICC and are interested in more offensive gearing options for their farm raids. Note that the <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-253/sanctified-lasherweave-battlegear">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sanctified Lasherweave Battlegear</span></a> set packs so much offensive power "for free", in addition to its survivability value, that itemizing specifically for Threat will never be necessary in ICC as long as you are executing the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/tank-rotation-cooldowns-abilities-pve#single-target-rotation">Threat rotation</a> properly and making use of your raid's <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=34477/misdirection">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_hunter_misdirection.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Misdirection</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=57934/tricks-of-the-trade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_tricksofthetrade.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tricks of the Trade</span></a> cooldowns for snap Threat. However, now that the stacking <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=73825/strength-of-wrynn">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bannerpvp_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Strength of Wrynn</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=73819/hellscreams-warsong">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_incinerate.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hellscream's Warsong</span></a> ICC zone buffs have ramped up to the 15% level, geared tanks no longer need to itemize exclusively for maximum survivability, and can justify some more balanced gearing choices in order to min-max their personal DPS on farm content. Not all offensive swaps are equally <i>efficient</i>, however, so quantitative simulation comparisons were used to optimize a balanced setup with the highest ratio of DPS gain to survivability loss relative to the maximum survival setup presented earlier in the guide:<br/>
