<br/>In order of most to least efficient, the following swaps can be made from the earlier maximum survival setup as your raid team becomes increasingly comfortable with Phase 4 raid encounters: <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50735/oathbinder-charge-of-the-ranger-general">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_staff_109.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Oathbinder, Charge of the Ranger-General</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=60692/enchant-chest-powerful-stats">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulagood_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Chest - Powerful Stats</span></a>, <img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/icons/horde.png"/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47546/sylvanas-cunning">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_18.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sylvanas' Cunning</span></a> /<wbr/> <img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/guide/images/27798.png"/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47545/vereesas-dexterity">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vereesa's Dexterity</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54576/signet-of-twilight">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_icecrownringc.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signet of Twilight</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55002/flexweave-underlay">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flexweave Underlay</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50604/band-of-the-bone-colossus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_83.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of the Bone Colossus</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50670/toskks-maximized-wristguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_41.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Toskk's Maximized Wristguards</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=54999/hyperspeed-accelerators">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hyperspeed Accelerators</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50728/lanathels-chain-of-flagellation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_necklace_50.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lana'thel's Chain of Flagellation</span></a>, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=41398/relentless-earthsiege-diamond">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_shadowspirit_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relentless Earthsiege Diamond</span></a>, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54590/sharpened-twilight-scale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubysanctum4.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sharpened Twilight Scale</span></a>. At the 15% power level of the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=73825/strength-of-wrynn">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bannerpvp_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Strength of Wrynn</span></a> buff, the example balanced setup above that makes all of these swaps achieves comparable survival rates in simulations of the Heroic Lich King encounter as the full survival setup without any zone buff, but with a ~2500 personal DPS improvement.<br/>
<br/>It is important to note that in contrast with the above offensive swaps, swapping in DPS gems in place of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40119/solid-majestic-zircon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_42.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Solid Majestic Zircon</span></a> gems is far less efficient at trading off survivability for damage, and is <i>not</i> recommended even at higher buff percentages in ICC. Likewise, the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=64571/blood-draining">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_bloodstone_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blood Draining</span></a> weapon enchant is so incredibly efficient at preventing tank deaths that it should not be dropped even in balanced setups like the one above.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="ruby-sanctum">Updates for Best in Slot Gear in Ruby Sanctum</h3>Unfortunately, <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4987/the-ruby-sanctum">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Ruby Sanctum</span></a> offers only a single pure survivability upgrade for Feral tanks relative to alternatives from <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> and prior raids: <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54580/umbrage-armbands">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_41.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Umbrage Armbands</span></a> off <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=39863/halion">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Halion</span></a> on 25-man Heroic difficulty. However, if your bear is already wearing <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50670/toskks-maximized-wristguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_41.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Toskk's Maximized Wristguards</span></a> and is geared enough to comfortably survive the Heroic Lich King encounter, then you can easily pass on <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54580/umbrage-armbands">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_41.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Umbrage Armbands</span></a>, since the new bracers are a DPS/<wbr/>TPS downgrade from Toskk's and offer only a minor survivability increase. In contrast, if you have not yet obtained <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50670/toskks-maximized-wristguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_41.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Toskk's Maximized Wristguards</span></a> and your raid team is still learning the Heroic Lich King encounter, then <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54580/umbrage-armbands">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_41.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Umbrage Armbands</span></a> are worth prioritizing for increased safety during progression.<br/>
<br/>For geared bears who have already been comfortably farming Heroic <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>, there are two other drops from <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4987/the-ruby-sanctum">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Ruby Sanctum</span></a> worth considering as offensive gear swaps: <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54576/signet-of-twilight">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_icecrownringc.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signet of Twilight</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54590/sharpened-twilight-scale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubysanctum4.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sharpened Twilight Scale</span></a>. These pieces are particularly efficient on hybrid fights like <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=37813/deathbringer-saurfang">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer Saurfang</span></a> and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36626/festergut">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Festergut</span></a>, where Ferals spend a significant fraction of time DPSing in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=768/cat-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a> while not actively tanking, but will be highly contested by pure DPS players.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Frost for Feral Druid Tank Phase 4</h3>As mentioned at the start of this guide, the most important gearing priority for Feral tanks at the start of Phase 4 will be completing the 4-piece <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-845/lasherweave-battlegear">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Lasherweave Battlegear</span></a> set bonus, so all of your initial <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> accumulation during the first month of the phase should go towards 251 Item Level Tier 10 pieces. Note that unlike the Tier 9 set in Phase 3, obtaining these base pieces from Emblems is a <i>prerequisite</i> to obtaining the upgraded 264 or 277 Item Level versions of each item from raid token drops, making it even more important to purchase all four pieces of 251 Tier as soon as possible. Many guilds are likely to give early priority on <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52028/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_judgementsofthejust.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> drops from 25-man ICC to their tanks in order to minimize wipes to tank deaths during progression, so you may easily find yourself in a scenario where you already have some of these tokens sitting in your bags, but cannot use them until you obtain more Emblems.<br/>
<br/>The optimal four pieces of Tier 10 to target for bear tanking are the helm, shoulder, glove, and leg slots. This is because the chest slot has the best available off-piece option across the five slots, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50656/ikfiruss-sack-of-wonder">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_22.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ikfirus's Sack of Wonder</span></a>, and is also accessible for all players since it drops from the easiest 25-man Heroic encounter (Gunship Battle). Among the other four slots, it is worth targeting <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51700/lasherweave-legguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_35.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lasherweave Legguards</span></a> as your first <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> purchase if you anticipate obtaining a <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> early on, since the 264 Item Level version of the legs will be the largest individual upgrade from the Phase 3 BiS option in that slot (<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46975/leggings-of-the-broken-beast">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leggings of the Broken Beast</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47420/legwraps-of-the-broken-beast">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_30a.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Legwraps of the Broken Beast</span></a>). The next Tier slot to target if you anticipate early <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> priority is the helm slot, since <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51143/sanctified-lasherweave-headguard">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_148.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sanctified Lasherweave Headguard</span></a> is also individually an upgrade over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48204/malfurions-headguard-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_139.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Malfurion's Headguard of Triumph</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48201/runetotems-headguard-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_145b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Runetotem's Headguard of Triumph</span></a> from Phase 3. The glove and shoulder pieces on the other hand are individually worse than Phase 3 alternatives even when upgraded using <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a>, and should only be equipped once you obtain all four pieces in order to activate the set bonus.<br/>
<br/>Once you have obtained all four Tier 10 pieces, the only remaining <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> rewards in the above BiS setups are <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50456/idol-of-the-crying-moon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_natureguardian.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Crying Moon</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50466/sentinels-winter-cloak">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sentinel's Winter Cloak</span></a>. The other rewards are all outclassed by 277 Item Level drops from 25-man Heroic ICC bosses, but can serve as solid intermediate upgrades while you are waiting for the BiS option to drop. In particular, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50356/corroded-skeleton-key">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_key_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corroded Skeleton Key</span></a> provides a hefty survivability increase over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a> from Phase 2-3, and is worth the investment unless you get lucky with an early <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50361/sindragosas-flawless-fang">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa's Flawless Fang</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50344/unidentifiable-organ">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ore_feliron_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unidentifiable Organ</span></a> drop.<br/>
