<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="feet">Feet for Feral Druid Tank Phase 4</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50607/frostbitten-fur-boots">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_leather_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frostbitten Fur Boots</span></a> are the clear winner in the boots slot for most ICC encounters, since they are the only 277 Item Level option available. But as you might expect, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=43592/polar-boots">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_cloth_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Polar Boots</span></a> will provide higher survivability than these when tanking <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36853/sindragosa">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa</span></a> specifically.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Feet Enchant</b>:  <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a>, requires <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=202/engineering">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a>.<br/>On top of its other PvE benefits, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=202/engineering">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> in WotLK also offers a uniquely powerful movement speed cooldown in the form of the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a> enchant, which gives <i>any pair of tanking boots</i> the same effect as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=23824/rocket-boots-xtreme">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gizmo_rocketboot_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rocket Boots Xtreme</span></a> from TBC! It cannot be overstated how much utility Nitro Boosts provide over the course of a competitive raid clear, whether by letting you zoom ahead of your raid group to initiate a pull and establish a Threat lead, or by unlocking raid strategies that would not be possible otherwise. If you are not an Engineer, then the best alternative boots enchant is <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47901/enchant-boots-tuskarrs-vitality">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulagood_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Boots - Tuskarr's Vitality</span></a>.<div class="pad"></div>
