<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="rings">Rings for Feral Druid Tank Phase 4</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50622/deviums-eternally-cold-ring">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_86.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Devium's Eternally Cold Ring</span></a> is by far the highest survivability tanking ring for Feral Druids in Phase 4 due to its excellent mix of Stamina and mitigation stats, and it should be permanently equipped while your raid team is still progressing through Hard Mode encounters.<br/>
<br/>The second ring slot is <i>much</i> lower impact by comparison. While <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50404/ashen-band-of-endless-courage">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_84.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ashen Band of Endless Courage</span></a> will be the highest value choice for most encounters, simulation comparisons indicate that it performs almost identically to both Phase 3 BiS survival rings (<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47955/loop-of-the-twin-valkyr">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_59.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Loop of the Twin Val'kyr</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49489/signified-ring-of-binding">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signified Ring of Binding</span></a>) for preventing tank deaths on hard hitting ICC bosses like <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36597/the-lich-king">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Lich King</span></a>, and the entirety of its value comes from its superior offensive stats. Importantly, the Ashen Band should only be equipped once you achieve Exalted reputation with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/faction=1156/the-ashen-verdict">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Ashen Verdict</span></a>, as it is strictly worse than both <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47955/loop-of-the-twin-valkyr">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_59.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Loop of the Twin Val'kyr</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49489/signified-ring-of-binding">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signified Ring of Binding</span></a> at Revered reputation or below.<br/>
<br/>When tanking <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36853/sindragosa">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50678/seal-of-many-mouths">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_icecrownringc.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Seal of Many Mouths</span></a> will provide higher survivability value than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50404/ashen-band-of-endless-courage">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_84.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ashen Band of Endless Courage</span></a> in the second ring slot by reducing the frequency of Parry Haste sequences without sacrificing too much physical EHP. However, the <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36627/rotface">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Rotface</span></a> ring will still be only a minor upgrade over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49489/signified-ring-of-binding">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signified Ring of Binding</span></a> from Phase 3 on this encounter.<br/>
<br/>At higher power levels of the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=73825/strength-of-wrynn">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bannerpvp_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Strength of Wrynn</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=73819/hellscreams-warsong">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_incinerate.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hellscream's Warsong</span></a> ICC zone buffs, geared bears can afford to swap in one or even two DPS rings in place of the above survival options in order to min-max their personal DPS on farm content. The most efficient offensive swaps in the ring slots are <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54576/signet-of-twilight">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_icecrownringc.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signet of Twilight</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50604/band-of-the-bone-colossus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_83.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of the Bone Colossus</span></a>, provided that you have enough Hit budget available in your gear set to accommodate the Hit Rating on these pieces without exceeding the cap.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Ring Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=59636/enchant-ring-stamina">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Ring - Stamina</span></a>, requires <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=333/enchanting">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchanting</span></a>. <br/>Only Enchanters may apply ring enchants on their own rings.<div class="pad"></div>
