<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="trinkets">Trinkets for Feral Druid Tank Phase 4</h3>Phase 4 introduces multiple new tanking trinkets for bears to choose from, but the surprising conclusion from extensive simulation optimizations is that the Phase 3 "Last Stand" trinket <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47451/juggernauts-vitality">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Juggernaut's Vitality</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a> continues to be hands down the top survivability option for the hardest hitting ICC bosses. As described in our <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/tank-bis-gear-pve-phase-3#trinkets">Phase 3 BiS guide</a>, Last Stand trinkets are extremely efficient for tank survival because they collapse a huge amount of effective Stamina into an on-use effect that you can activate precisely when you need the extra health. ICC encounters play directly into this strength, since the damage profiles of the hardest hitting bosses in the raid center around timed "tank buster" abilities that require pre-planned personal and external cooldown rotations for the active tank in order to consistently survive the burst damage. As a result, even though <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a> provides lower passive Stamina than higher item level Phase 4 options like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50356/corroded-skeleton-key">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_key_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corroded Skeleton Key</span></a>, it <i>effectively</i> contributes a whopping 533 Stamina when incorporated into a CD rotation for tank busters like <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36853/sindragosa">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa</span></a>'s <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69649/frost-breath">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostnova.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Breath</span></a> and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36597/the-lich-king">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Lich King</span></a>'s <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69409/soul-reaper">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_shadowdance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Reaper</span></a>. The trinket's on-use effect is so overpowered for ICC boss damage profiles that even the 245 Item Level Normal version (which can be farmed in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/news/wrath-classic-3-4-3-ptr-defilers-scourgestone-wotlk-classic-334787">Titan Rune Gamma dungeons</a> next phase) will outperform Phase 4 alternatives.<br/>
<br/>The best new Phase 4 tank trinket to pair with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47451/juggernauts-vitality">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Juggernaut's Vitality</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a> when optimizing for survivability is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50364/sindragosas-flawless-fang">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa's Flawless Fang</span></a>. This trinket not only provides the highest passive Stamina of all available options, but also contributes its own overpowered on-use effect, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71638/aegis-of-dalaran">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_antimagicshell.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Aegis of Dalaran</span></a>, which complements the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67753/fortitude">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_mindvision.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fortitude</span></a> buff from <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a> due to its much shorter 1 minute cooldown. Having access to a 10-second duration Shadow Resistance cooldown every minute is particularly impactful for Heroic Lich King progression, since <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69409/soul-reaper">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_shadowdance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Reaper</span></a> is cast around once every 30 seconds, and its initial application damage (which often one-shots under-geared tanks since it can batch with a prior melee swing) is partially resistible.<br/>
<br/>You may notice that not even a single non-Stamina-boosting trinket made the cut for the viable tanking options in the below list. This is a consequence of the consistently slow boss swing timers across ICC encounters, which favors EHP over avoidance stats for tank survivability, combined with the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69127/chill-of-the-throne">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_zone_icecrown_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chill of the Throne</span></a> debuff that further diminishes the value of avoidance due to its nonlinear scaling. The fact that the deadliest tank buster abilities in the raid deal magical damage fully seals the deal in favor of Stamina trinkets.<div class="pad"></div>
